🚽 Test case: round-21 review finding #3 -- making `skibidi` reachable
🚽 through the whole `type` grammar (round 20) meant validity needed
🚽 patching at every declaration-like position, not just variable
🚽 declarations. A named by-value (pointer_level 0) void parameter is
🚽 nonsense -- an empty parameter list already spells "no parameters" --
🚽 but param_list's grammar action had no check for it, so
🚽 `rizz wat(skibidi x)` parsed and installed `x` into the symbol table
🚽 with type VAR_VOID. Now rejected at parse time.
rizz wat(skibidi x) {
    bussin 42;
}

skibidi main {
    bussin 0;
}
